Z||000000||vtom||11-02-2000||12:00 PM||||I have purchased a '84 SE that had set for the last 3 years but was in great shape except for the 4 popper, in it was frozen.<BR>Itjust so happened that I have a '86 parts car that had a great V6 in it.  After a week of changing machanicals over it came to the point of trying to start it up.  Well surprize, no power for anything.  Is there that much difference in the wiring harness between the two years?  Do I have to change out the wiring between the two cars. Is there any easy way? HELP!<P>Thanks<BR>vtom||||reg||9
Z||000001||william_thorniii||11-02-2000||12:40 PM||||vtom,<P>There is so much difference between the two cars that I find it difficult to believe you got it wired at all.  The method that you should have taken was to replace the engine, ECM and wiring harness from the donor car into the 84.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
